From: MCC45TR <mcc45tr@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Restore pending idle actions after an interactive resume

The AC state may stay unchanged across suspend, and no idle-resume event is
guaranteed after lid/button wake. In that case DimDisplay/DPMS keep keyboard
brightness at zero until an unrelated configuration change. Dispatch their
existing restoration path after all resume slots have cleared suspend state.
Background wakes retain the existing display/backlight policy. No polling or
profile reload; the actions keep ownership of their saved brightness and zero.
Based on KDE PowerDevil v6.8.3, GPL-2.0-or-later.

diff --git a/daemon/powerdevilcore.cpp b/daemon/powerdevilcore.cpp
--- a/daemon/powerdevilcore.cpp
+++ b/daemon/powerdevilcore.cpp
@@ -1002,6 +1002,16 @@ void Core::onResumeFromSuspend() {
     emitBatteryChargePercentNotification(percent, 1000);
 
     m_batteryController->updateAcAdapterState();
+
+    // Let action-specific resume slots clear their suspend flags first.
+    // A physical wake must restore pending DimDisplay/DPMS brightness even
+    // when AC/profile values did not change and no input event is delivered.
+    const auto wakeup = m_suspendController->lastWakeupType();
+    if (!(wakeup & SuspendController::WakeupSource::Timer)
+        && !(wakeup & SuspendController::WakeupSource::Telephony)
+        && !(wakeup & SuspendController::WakeupSource::Network)) {
+        QTimer::singleShot(0, this, &Core::onResumingFromIdle);
+    }
 }
 
 void Core::readChargeThreshold()
